{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured `/srv/inventory` as a persistent bind mount at `/mnt/inventory`. It remained mounted with intact data after node1 rebooted exactly once.","actions_performed":["Created `/srv/inventory` and `/mnt/inventory`.","Added `/srv/inventory /mnt/inventory none bind 0 0` to `/etc/fstab`.","Activated and verified the bind mount using matching source/target data and inode identity.","Rebooted node1 once and verified its boot ID changed and the mount recovered."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Persistent bind mount at `/mnt/inventory`","command_ids":["cmd-2022d0088c524cb3","cmd-b06ea8342671453d"],"summary":"Before and after reboot, `/etc/fstab` contained the bind entry, `/mnt/inventory` was an active mount backed by `/srv/inventory`, and both paths exposed matching data and inode identity."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-2022d0088c524cb3","cmd-650c66cfa4b2434e","cmd-b06ea8342671453d"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID was `6693787a-bc30-4853-8c5b-57dc30031b19`; the reboot was acknowledged; afterward the boot ID was `3bab384c-6f4c-4e31-b01c-6381798de1e9`, with the mount unit active and persisted data readable."}]}
